#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364921 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3497c02b-4c62-58d9-8c73-ee1a1142c429" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Rate of Change of a Leg Using the Pythagorean Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5aaf26ff-d797-5b88-ad8d-e6959ba6a72a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.7\\,\\text{km/h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364923} {:answer/id #uuid "08c96085-1bec-508c-8887-647747724f28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\,\\text{km/h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364924} {:answer/id #uuid "3f4ab70c-0e95-599d-840b-1e1058885e87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.8\\,\\text{km/h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364925} {:answer/id #uuid "ae5c7ed9-0861-5f60-8281-0cedacc28ee1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.1\\,\\text{km/h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364926} {:answer/id #uuid "56b2c2b2-4829-5aa6-968d-cb46970d071d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.9\\,\\text{km/h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364927}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "56b2c2b2-4829-5aa6-968d-cb46970d071d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.9\\,\\text{km/h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364927} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5b0c1f8-5a20-5aeb-bf37-af86c048ed37" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364922}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a3e3f798-ab0c-5122-879a-c6328e19834f" :question/math-academy-id "q-103792" :question/problem "James and Mary have a date at the cinema theater.\nJames arrived at the agreed time, but Mary is late. After $20$ minutes of waiting, James decides to go home.\n\nJames travels north from the theater with a speed of $3.2\\,\\text{km/h}.$ Mary travels west toward the theater. When James is $0.8\\,\\text{km}$ from the theater, Mary is $1.5\\,\\text{km}$ from the theater. If the distance between them increases at a speed of $2.3\\,\\text{km/h},$ what is Mary's speed?" :question/worked-solution "We start by drawing a diagram of the problem.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069977/assets/1728c9ca91ef28b19c28048f5a640d0eebbd08f504bb594bc978277fe5620d70.png)\n\nIn the diagram,\n\n- $x$ is the distance between Mary and the cinema theater,\n\n- $y$ is the distance between James and the cinema theater,\n\n- $z$ is the distance between James and Mary.\n\nAs shown in the diagram, $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ form a right triangle with $z$ as the hypotenuse. We wish to find the rate of change of $x,$ which is $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}.$ \n\nWe know that $x=1.5\\,\\text{km}$ and $y=0.8\\,\\text{km}.$ We can find $z$ using the Pythagorean Theorem, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={z}^{2} \\\\ {1.5}^{2}+{0.8}^{2} & ={z}^{2} \\\\ {z}^{2} & =2.89 \\\\ z & =1.7\\,\\text{km}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also know that:\n\n- $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=3.2\\,\\text{km}/\\text{h},$\n\n- $\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}=2.3\\,\\text{km}/\\text{h}.$\n\nFinally, we differentiate both sides of ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}={z}^{2}$ with respect to $t$ and then substitute in the known values, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({z}^{2}) \\\\ 2x\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =2z\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t} \\\\ 2(1.5)\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+2(0.8)(3.2) & =2(1.7)(2.3) \\\\ 3\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =7.82-5.12 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =0.9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, Mary is approaching the cinema theater with a speed of $0.9\\,\\text{km/h}.$"}]}
